## Authentication APIs

### POST /auth/register
- **Purpose:** Register a new user
- **Request body:**
```json
{
  "username": "john_doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "securePassword123",
  "role": "Learner"
}
```
- **Response:**
```json
{
  "username": "john_doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "role": "Learner"
}
```

### POST /auth/login
- **Purpose:** Authenticate a user and receive a bearer token
- **Request body:**
```json
{
  "username": "john_doe",
  "password": "securePassword123"
}
```
- **Response:**
```json
{
  "access_token": "jwt_token_here",
  "token_type": "bearer"
}
```

### GET /auth/me
- **Purpose:** Retrieve the currently authenticated user
- **Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- **Response:**
```json
{
  "sub": "john_doe",
  "role": "Learner",
  "exp": 1700000000
}
```

