## Course APIs

### POST /courses
- **Purpose:** Create a new course
- **Authorization:** Instructor only
- **Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- **Request body:**
```json
{
  "title": "Intro to Sign Language",
  "description": "Beginner course covering basics",
  "instructor_id": "1"
}
```
- **Response:**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Intro to Sign Language",
  "description": "Beginner course covering basics",
  "instructor_id": "1"
}
```

### GET /courses
- **Purpose:** Retrieve all courses
- **Response:**
```json
[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "title": "Intro to Sign Language",
    "description": "Beginner course covering basics",
    "instructor_id": "1"
  }
]
```

### GET /courses/{course_id}
- **Purpose:** Retrieve a course by ID
- **Response:**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Intro to Sign Language",
  "description": "Beginner course covering basics",
  "instructor_id": "1"
}
```

### PUT /courses/{course_id}
- **Purpose:** Update a course
- **Authorization:** Instructor only
- **Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- **Request body:**
```json
{
  "title": "Intro to Sign Language - Updated",
  "description": "Updated description"
}
```
- **Response:**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Intro to Sign Language - Updated",
  "description": "Updated description",
  "instructor_id": "1"
}
```

### DELETE /courses/{course_id}
- **Purpose:** Delete a course
- **Authorization:** Admin only
- **Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- **Response:**
```json
{
  "message": "Course deleted"
}
```

---

## Authentication

- Uses JWT bearer tokens
- The token is generated by `POST /auth/login`
- Protected endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`

## Notes

- `POST /auth/register` creates a user with `username`, `email`, `password`, and `role`
- `POST /auth/login` accepts `username` and `password`
- `/auth/me`, `/courses`, and course modification routes require bearer auth
- Role checks are enforced by `services.rbac.role_required`
